  "result": "`Cart.remove('sku-1')` now removes the Widget line, and all 6 tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** in `shop/models.py:33`, `Cart.remove` checked each line's item name instead of its SKU. In the demo the name is `'Widget'`, which never equals `'sku-1'`, so nothing was removed and `count()` returned 2.\n\n**Fix:** the check now uses the item's `sku` field, the same one `Cart.add` uses.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1`.\n- pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the suite with `python3 -m unittest` instead.\n- None of the existing tests cover `Cart.remove`, so the demo is the only check of the fix. I haven't added a regression test; I can if you'd like one.",
